          "In the UK many studios map these phases onto the **RIBA Plan of Work 2020**, which architects also use, so both teams talk about the same stages. The BIID Interior Design Project Book, published by RIBA Publishing with the British Institute of Interior Design, sets out a designer's obligations at each stage and reflects the 2020 Plan of Work. See our [architecture project management](/project-management/industries/architecture-project-management/) guide for the RIBA stages and their rough AIA equivalents.",
          "On UK office projects you will also hear **Cat A** (the landlord's base fit-out with floors, ceilings, basic lighting and services) and **Cat B** (the tenant's fit-out: partitions, meeting rooms, kitchens, furniture and branding). Interior designers usually lead Cat B design.",
